          "title": "Sentences to take to the pharmacy",
          "items": [
            "**אֲנִי לֹא מַרְגִּישׁ / מַרְגִּישָׁה טוֹב** — I don't feel well.",
            "**כּוֹאֵב לִי ...** — my ... hurts. Just add the body part.",
            "**יֵשׁ לִי חֹם / שִׁעוּל / נַזֶּלֶת** — I have a fever / a cough / a runny nose.",
            "**יֵשׁ לִי אֲלֶרְגְיָה לְ...** — I'm allergic to...",
            "**זֶה בְּלִי מִרְשָׁם?** — is this without a prescription?",
            "**כַּמָּה פְּעָמִים בְּיוֹם?** — how many times a day?",
            "**זֶה דָּחוּף** *(zeh dakhuf)* — it's urgent."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "⚠️ **Israeli emergency numbers: 101 for an ambulance (מָגֵן דָּוִד אָדֹם), 100 police, 102 fire.** Sentences to know without thinking: **צָרִיךְ אַמְבּוּלַנְס!** *(tsarikh ambulans)* and **קִרְאוּ לְרוֹפֵא!** *(kir'u lerofe — call a doctor!)*."
        }
